('Level4_2','Level4_2_3191','sicken','''sɪkən','''sɪk(ə)n','[v] 使患病；使恶心；使嫌恶','The notion that art should be controlled by intellectuals sickened him.  艺术应该由知识分子掌控的观念使他很厌恶。'),
('Level4_2','Level4_2_3192','sickle','''sɪkl','''sɪk(ə)l','[n] 镰刀','He swished the tops off weeds with a sickle.  他挥动镰刀嗖嗖地割掉了杂草的草尖。'),
('Level4_2','Level4_2_3193','sideboard','''saɪd''bɔrd','''saɪdbɔːd','[n] 餐具柜；侧板，边线界墙',''),
